From: Lance Yang <lance.yang@linux.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:19:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mm: fix deferred split queue races during migration

commit 3bac01168982ec3e3bf87efdc1807c7933590a85 upstream.

[ Backport: 6.12 deferred_split_scan() keeps unhandled folios on a local
  list and splices them back. Put the requeue label on the branch that
  keeps a folio on that list, so a folio that fails folio_trylock() stays
  queued. Comments adapted to that layout. ]

migrate_folio_move() records the deferred split queue state from src and
replays it on dst.  Replaying it after remove_migration_ptes(src, dst, 0)
makes dst visible before it is requeued, so a concurrent rmap-removal path
can mark dst partially mapped and trip the WARN in deferred_split_folio().

Move the requeue before remove_migration_ptes() so dst is back on the
deferred split queue before it becomes visible again.

Because migration still holds dst locked at that point, teach
deferred_split_scan() to requeue a folio when folio_trylock() fails.
Otherwise a fully mapped underused folio can be dequeued by the shrinker
and silently lost from split_queue.

[ziy@nvidia.com: move the comment]
